  "slot-milling": {
    "changes": [
      {
        "before": "<p>In the fast-paced landscape of contemporary manufacturing, slot milling plays a pivotal role by facilitating the creation of complex, high-tolerance components that meet the stringent demands of modern engineering. It&#8217;s especially crucial in sectors where reliable part assembly and performance are non-negotiable, such as aerospace for structural reinforcements, automotive for drivetrain integrations, and electronics for circuit board housings. The advent of advanced CNC technologies has further elevated slot milling&#8217;s importance, enabling greater efficiency through optimized toolpaths, reduced material waste via precise cuts, and the ability to handle intricate designs that were once prohibitively time-consuming.</p>",
        "after": "<p>In the fast-paced landscape of contemporary manufacturing, slot milling plays a pivotal role by facilitating the creation of complex, high-tolerance components that meet the stringent demands of modern engineering. It&#8217;s especially crucial in sectors where reliable part assembly and performance are non-negotiable, such as aerospace for structural reinforcements, <a href=\"/industries/automotive\">automotive</a> for drivetrain integrations, and electronics for circuit board housings. The advent of advanced CNC technologies has further elevated slot milling&#8217;s importance, enabling greater efficiency through optimized toolpaths, reduced material waste via precise cuts, and the ability to handle intricate designs that were once prohibitively time-consuming.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "appendHtml": "<p>For a component example, review the drawing requirements for <a href=\"/custom-cnc-parts/motor-shaft\">motor shafts with machined features</a>.</p>",
    "insertionBefore": null
  },
  "thread-milling-vs-tapping": {
    "changes": [
      {
        "before": "<p>Thread milling and tapping are two essential machining processes used to create threads in materials, particularly metals. Threads are spiral grooves that allow screws, bolts, and other fasteners to secure components together. While both methods achieve similar results, they differ significantly in their approaches, tools, and applications. Thread milling involves a specialized cutter that interpolates around the hole on a CNC machine, offering precision and flexibility. In contrast, tapping uses a tap tool that rotates directly into the hole, mimicking a screw&#8217;s action. </p>",
        "after": "<p>Thread milling and tapping are two essential machining processes used to create threads in materials, particularly metals. Threads are spiral grooves that allow screws, bolts, and other <a href=\"/blog/fastener-machining\">fasteners</a> to secure components together. While both methods achieve similar results, they differ significantly in their approaches, tools, and applications. Thread milling involves a specialized cutter that interpolates around the hole on a CNC machine, offering precision and flexibility. In contrast, tapping uses a tap tool that rotates directly into the hole, mimicking a screw&#8217;s action. </p>"
      }
    ],
    "appendHtml": "<p>For components combining turned diameters and internal threads, review our <a href=\"/services/cnc-turning-and-milling\">CNC turning and milling service</a> with the part drawing, material, quantity, and inspection requirements.</p><p>For a component example, review the drawing requirements for <a href=\"/custom-cnc-parts/threaded-bushing\">custom threaded bushings</a>.</p>",
    "insertionBefore": null
  },
  "what-is-a-cnc-lathe": {
    "changes": [
      {
        "before": "<p>A CNC lathe is a precision machine tool that automates the turning process to create cylindrical parts with high accuracy. By rotating the workpiece against a stationary cutting tool, it removes material to form shapes like shafts, bushings, and pipes. CNC stands for Computer Numerical Control, meaning the machine follows digital instructions for consistent results. These lathes are essential in industries requiring rotational symmetry, handling materials such as metals, plastics, and composites. This guide covers how CNC lathes work, their types, differences from other machines, applications, design tips, and more. For instant insights into related services, check our <a class=\"blog-post-link\" href=\"/services\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">CNC Machining Services</a>.</p>",
        "after": "<p>A CNC lathe is a precision machine tool that automates the <a href=\"/blog/cnc-turning\">turning</a> process to create cylindrical parts with high accuracy. By rotating the workpiece against a stationary cutting tool, it removes material to form shapes like shafts, bushings, and pipes. CNC stands for Computer Numerical Control, meaning the machine follows digital instructions for consistent results. These lathes are essential in industries requiring rotational symmetry, handling materials such as metals, plastics, and composites. This guide covers how CNC lathes work, their types, differences from other machines, applications, design tips, and more. For instant insights into related services, check our <a class=\"blog-post-link\" href=\"/services\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">CNC Machining Services</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "appendHtml": "<p>For a component example, review the drawing requirements for <a href=\"/custom-cnc-parts/swiss-machined-parts\">Swiss machined components</a>.</p>",
    "insertionBefore": null
  },
